Looking at the code fragments and the function signature, I need to implement `test_graph_reset_node` that tests the reset functionality of observer nodes. Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#pragma once

#include <reaction/core/observer_node.h>
#include <reaction/graph/observer_graph.h>
#include <memory>
#include <string>

namespace test_reaction {

class ResetAwareNode : public reaction::ObserverNode {
public:
    explicit ResetAwareNode(std::string name) 
        : m_name(std::move(name)), m_notificationCount(0) {
    }

    int notifications() const {
        return m_notificationCount;
    }

    void clear() {
        m_notificationCount = 0;
    }

protected:
    void onNotify() override {
        m_notificationCount++;
    }

private:
    std::string m_name;
    int m_notificationCount;
};

struct ResetNodeResult {
    bool notifiedBeforeReset;
    bool notifiedAfterReset;
};

ResetNodeResult test_graph_reset_node(const std::string &sourceName,
                                      const std::string &targetName) {
    // 1. Create source and target ResetAwareNode instances
    auto source = std::make_shared<ResetAwareNode>(sourceName);
    auto target = std::make_shared<ResetAwareNode>(targetName);

    // 2. Get observer graph instance
    auto &graph = reaction::ObserverGraph::getInstance();

    // 3. Register nodes
    graph.addNode(source);
    graph.addNode(target);

    // 4. Set up observer relationship
    graph.addObserver(source, target);

    // 5. Trigger notification on source
    source->notifyObservers();

    // 6. Check if target was notified before reset
    bool notifiedBeforeReset = target->notifications() > 0;

    // 7. Clear target notification count
    target->clear();

    // 8. Reset target node
    graph.resetNode(target);

    // 9. Trigger notification on source again
    source->notifyObservers();

    // 10. Check if target was notified after reset
    bool notifiedAfterReset = target->notifications() > 0;

    // 11. Close nodes
    graph.closeNode(source);
    graph.closeNode(target);

    // 12. Return reset node result
    return ResetNodeResult{notifiedBeforeReset, notifiedAfterReset};
}

}  // namespace test_reaction
```

This implementation:

1. Creates two `ResetAwareNode` instances with custom names
2. Gets the singleton `ObserverGraph` instance
3. Registers both nodes with the graph
4. Sets up an observer relationship where target observes source
5. Notifies observers from the source to trigger target
6. Checks if target received notification (should be true)
7. Clears the notification counter on target
8. Resets the target node (breaking observer relationships)
9. Triggers another notification from source
10. Checks if target was notified after reset (should be false since relationship was broken)
11. Properly closes both nodes to clean up
12. Returns a result struct containing both notification states

The `ResetAwareNode` class extends `ObserverNode` and tracks notification counts, implementing the `onNotify()` method to increment the counter when notifications are received.

