1. Enables monitoring using `setMonitoringEnabled(true)`
2. Initializes the stack monitor with `initialize()`
3. Gets initial usage stats with `getUsageStats()`
4. Checks template-based allocation with `canAllocate<large_size>()`
5. Checks runtime allocation with `canAllocate(large_size)`
6. Creates a large `StackGuard` instance
7. Checks if the guard succeeded with `success()`
8. Tests if allocation is blocked by trying to allocate more than remaining space
9. Gets final usage stats
10. Returns the snapshot (the guard destructor will automatically release the stack)

